# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Documentation for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Dokumentasi untuk versi terbaru Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) {#sample-based-quantum-diagonalization-sqd}"
msgstr "Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) {#sample-based-quantum-diagonalization-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package implements sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) — a technique for finding eigenvalues and eigenvectors of quantum operators, such as a quantum system Hamiltonian [\\[1–6\\]](#references). It can target Hamiltonians expressed as linear combinations of Pauli operators or second-quantized Fermionic operators. SQD-based workflows can be run on current quantum computers and have been shown to scale to problem sizes beyond what was possible with variational methods — and even beyond the reach of exact classical diagonalization methods.\n"
msgstr "Paket ini mengimplementasikan sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) — teknik untuk mencari eigenvalue dan eigenvector dari operator kuantum, seperti Hamiltonian sistem kuantum [\\[1–6\\]](#references). Teknik ini bisa menargetkan Hamiltonian yang dinyatakan sebagai kombinasi linear operator Pauli atau operator Fermionic terkuantisasi-kedua. Alur kerja berbasis SQD bisa dijalankan di komputer kuantum saat ini dan terbukti skalabel hingga ukuran masalah yang tidak mungkin dicapai metode variasional — bahkan melampaui jangkauan metode diagonalisasi klasik yang eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQD-based workflows involve first preparing one or more quantum states on a quantum device and sampling from them. Then, classical distributed computing is used to process those noisy samples. This processing occurs iteratively in two steps: first, a configuration recovery step corrects noisy samples using information about the input problem; second, the Hamiltonian is projected and diagonalized in the subspace spanned by those samples. These steps are repeated self-consistently until convergence. The result is an approximated lowest eigenvalue (energy) and lowest energy eigenstate of a given Hamiltonian. SQD is robust to samples corrupted by quantum noise; in fact, as long as a useful signal can be retrieved out of the quantum computer, the outcome of SQD will be insensitive to noisy bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Alur kerja berbasis SQD diawali dengan menyiapkan satu atau lebih keadaan kuantum di perangkat kuantum dan mengambil sampel darinya. Lalu, komputasi terdistribusi klasik dipakai untuk memproses sampel berderau tersebut. Pemrosesan ini terjadi secara iteratif dalam dua langkah: pertama, langkah pemulihan konfigurasi mengoreksi sampel berderau memakai informasi tentang masalah input; kedua, Hamiltonian diproyeksikan dan didiagonalisasi di subruang yang direntang oleh sampel tersebut. Langkah-langkah ini diulang secara self-consistent sampai konvergen. Hasilnya adalah aproksimasi eigenvalue terendah (energi) dan eigenstate berenergi terendah dari Hamiltonian tertentu. SQD tahan terhadap sampel yang rusak akibat derau kuantum; bahkan, selama sinyal yang berguna bisa diambil dari komputer kuantum, hasil SQD tidak akan terpengaruh oleh bitstring berderau.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit-addon-sqd` can be used to classically process samples drawn from a variety of quantum circuits in practice. For example:\n"
msgstr "`qiskit-addon-sqd` dalam praktiknya bisa dipakai untuk memproses secara klasik sampel yang diambil dari berbagai circuit kuantum. Misalnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> 1.  A variational circuit ansatz with parameters chosen such that sampling the circuit produces electronic configurations on which the target wavefunction (for example, the ground state) has significant support. This is appealing for chemistry applications where Hamiltonians can have millions of interaction terms [\\[1\\]](#references). For an example of this approach applied to chemistry using an LUCJ circuit, see the [tutorial for approximating the ground state energy of the N2 molecule](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
"> 2.  A set of Krylov basis states are prepared over increasing time intervals. Assuming a good initial state and sparsity of the ground state, this approach is proven to converge efficiently. As one needs to prepare Trotterized time evolution circuits on a quantum device, this approach is best for applications to lattice models [\\[2\\]](#references) instead of complex many-body Hamiltonians like those for quantum chemistry. For an example of this approach applied to Fermionic lattice Hamiltonians, see the [tutorial for approximating the ground state energy of a simplified single-impurity Anderson model](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
"> 3.  A set of Krylov basis states implemented with qDRIFT randomized compilation of the time evolution operator. This approach yields shorter-depth circuits compared to Trotter-based decompositions of the time evolution and so can be used for quantum chemistry Hamiltonians. This technique has been applied to the ground state energy of polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons [\\[6\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"> 1.  Ansatz circuit variasional dengan parameter yang dipilih sedemikian rupa sehingga sampling circuit menghasilkan konfigurasi elektronik yang menjadi support signifikan bagi fungsi gelombang target (misalnya ground state). Ini menarik untuk aplikasi kimia di mana Hamiltonian bisa punya jutaan suku interaksi [\\[1\\]](#references). Untuk contoh pendekatan ini yang diterapkan pada kimia memakai circuit LUCJ, lihat [tutorial untuk mengaproksimasi energi ground state molekul N2](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
"> 2.  Sekumpulan keadaan basis Krylov disiapkan pada interval waktu yang makin besar. Dengan asumsi keadaan awal yang baik dan sparsity pada ground state, pendekatan ini terbukti konvergen secara efisien. Karena perlu menyiapkan circuit evolusi waktu Trotterized di perangkat kuantum, pendekatan ini paling cocok untuk aplikasi pada model kisi [\\[2\\]](#references), bukan Hamiltonian many-body kompleks seperti yang ada di kimia kuantum. Untuk contoh pendekatan ini yang diterapkan pada Hamiltonian kisi Fermionic, lihat [tutorial untuk mengaproksimasi energi ground state model Anderson satu-pengotor yang disederhanakan](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
"> 3.  Sekumpulan keadaan basis Krylov yang diimplementasikan dengan kompilasi acak qDRIFT pada operator evolusi waktu. Pendekatan ini menghasilkan circuit berkedalaman lebih pendek dibandingkan dekomposisi evolusi waktu berbasis Trotter sehingga bisa dipakai untuk Hamiltonian kimia kuantum. Teknik ini telah diterapkan pada energi ground state hidrokarbon aromatik polisiklik [\\[6\\]](#references).\n"

