# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "System sizes and computational requirements {#system-sizes-and-computational-requirements}"
msgstr "Ukuran sistem dan kebutuhan komputasi {#system-sizes-and-computational-requirements}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The computational cost of SQD is dominated by the eigenstate solver calls. At each step of the self-consistent configuration recovery iteration, n\\_batches of eigenstate solver calls are performed. The different calls are embarrassingly parallel. In this [tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization), those calls are inside a for loop. **It is highly recommended to perform these calls in parallel**.\n"
msgstr "Biaya komputasi SQD didominasi oleh pemanggilan eigenstate solver. Di setiap langkah iterasi self-consistent configuration recovery, dilakukan n\\_batches pemanggilan eigenstate solver. Pemanggilan-pemanggilan itu bisa dijalankan secara paralel dengan mudah (embarrassingly parallel). Di [tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization) ini, pemanggilan tersebut ada di dalam sebuah for loop. **Sangat disarankan untuk menjalankan pemanggilan ini secara paralel**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion\") function is multithreaded and capable of handling systems with \\~25 spacial orbitals and \\~10 electrons with subspace dimensions of \\~\\$10^7\\$, using \\~10-30 cores.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_fermion\") bersifat multithreaded dan mampu menangani sistem dengan \\~25 orbital spasial dan \\~10 elektron dengan dimensi subruang \\~\\$10^7\\$, memakai \\~10-30 core.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing subspace dimensions {#choosing-subspace-dimensions}"
msgstr "Memilih dimensi subruang {#choosing-subspace-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of the subspace dimension affects the accuracy and runtime of the eigenstate solver. The larger the subspace, the more accurate the calculation, at the cost of increasing the runtime and memory requirements. The optimal subspace size of a given system is not known; thus, a convergence study with the subspace dimension can be performed, as described in this [guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension).\n"
msgstr "Pilihan dimensi subruang memengaruhi akurasi dan waktu jalan eigenstate solver. Makin besar subruangnya, makin akurat perhitungannya, tapi runtime dan kebutuhan memorinya juga naik. Ukuran subruang yang optimal untuk sistem tertentu belum diketahui; karena itu, kamu bisa melakukan studi konvergensi terhadap dimensi subruang, seperti dijelaskan di [panduan](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bounding the subspace dimension {#bounding-the-subspace-dimension}"
msgstr "Membatasi dimensi subruang {#bounding-the-subspace-dimension}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `samples_per_batch` argument of [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") sets the number of bitstrings contained in each batch, and thereby controls the subspace dimension indirectly: in the case of quantum chemistry applications, its value sets an upper bound to the subspace dimension. The dimension that actually results depends on how many of the sampled bitstrings are distinct, and it grows over the course of the self-consistent configuration recovery iterations, so it is not known in advance. See this [example](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-closed-shell) for more details.\n"
msgstr "Argumen `samples_per_batch` dari [`qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") menentukan jumlah bitstring di setiap batch, sehingga mengontrol dimensi subruang secara tidak langsung: untuk aplikasi kimia kuantum, nilainya menjadi batas atas dimensi subruang. Dimensi yang benar-benar dihasilkan bergantung pada berapa banyak bitstring hasil sampling yang berbeda, dan dimensi ini bertambah selama iterasi self-consistent configuration recovery, jadi tidak bisa diketahui sebelumnya. Lihat [contoh](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-closed-shell) ini untuk detail lebih lanjut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `max_dim` argument of the same function bounds the dimension directly, by limiting the number of CI strings retained in each spin sector. Since the subspace is spanned by the Cartesian product of the two spin sectors, `max_dim=d` caps the subspace dimension at `d**2`, while a tuple `max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` limits the spin-alpha and spin-beta sectors separately, capping the subspace dimension at `d_a * d_b` (with `symmetrize_spin=True`, the two limits must be equal). When a batch yields more CI strings than the limit allows, the strings requested through `include_configurations` and those carried over from the previous iteration are retained preferentially, and the remaining slots are filled with the most frequently sampled strings. Because it caps the size of the largest diagonalization that the eigenstate solver will be asked to perform, `max_dim` is a convenient way to keep the solver within a runtime and memory budget. See this [guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) for more details.\n"
msgstr "Argumen `max_dim` dari fungsi yang sama membatasi dimensi secara langsung, dengan membatasi jumlah string CI yang dipertahankan di tiap sektor spin. Karena subruang direntang oleh hasil kali Kartesius dari dua sektor spin, `max_dim=d` membatasi dimensi subruang di `d**2`, sedangkan tuple `max_dim=(d_a, d_b)` membatasi sektor spin-alpha dan spin-beta secara terpisah, sehingga dimensi subruang dibatasi di `d_a * d_b` (dengan `symmetrize_spin=True`, kedua batas harus sama). Ketika sebuah batch menghasilkan lebih banyak string CI daripada yang diizinkan batas, string yang diminta lewat `include_configurations` dan yang dibawa dari iterasi sebelumnya dipertahankan lebih dulu, lalu sisa slot diisi dengan string yang paling sering di-sampling. Karena membatasi ukuran diagonalisasi terbesar yang akan diminta dari eigenstate solver, `max_dim` adalah cara praktis untuk menjaga solver tetap dalam anggaran runtime dan memori. Lihat [panduan](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/choose-subspace-dimension) ini untuk detail lebih lanjut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solvers {#solvers}"
msgstr "Solver {#solvers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The projection and diagonalization steps are performed by a classical solver. We provide here two generic solvers, one for Fermionic systems and another for qubit systems. Other solvers that might be more efficient for specific systems can be interfaced by the users.\n"
msgstr "Langkah proyeksi dan diagonalisasi dilakukan oleh solver klasik. Di sini kami menyediakan dua solver generik, satu untuk sistem Fermionic dan satu lagi untuk sistem qubit. Solver lain yang mungkin lebih efisien untuk sistem tertentu bisa dihubungkan oleh pengguna.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trim SQD {#trim-sqd}"
msgstr "Trim SQD {#trim-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Standard SQD diagonalizes each subsampled batch independently and keeps the best result, so the number of configurations it can consider is limited to what one affordable subspace can hold. **Trim SQD** instead partitions the bitstrings into batches, performs an intermediate diagonalization of each batch, then performs a larger diagonalization using the highest-weight determinants from each partition. This method is based on joint research from the Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, and IBM [\\[7\\]](#references), and can be enabled by passing a [`TrimPolicy`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/trim#qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy \"qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy\") object to the [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") function.\n"
msgstr "SQD standar mendiagonalisasi setiap batch hasil subsampling secara independen dan menyimpan hasil terbaik, sehingga jumlah konfigurasi yang bisa dipertimbangkan terbatas pada apa yang muat di satu subruang yang terjangkau. **Trim SQD** justru mempartisi bitstring ke dalam beberapa batch, melakukan diagonalisasi perantara pada tiap batch, lalu melakukan diagonalisasi yang lebih besar memakai determinan berbobot tertinggi dari tiap partisi. Metode ini didasarkan pada riset bersama dari Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, dan IBM [\\[7\\]](#references), dan bisa diaktifkan dengan memberikan objek [`TrimPolicy`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/trim#qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy \"qiskit_addon_sqd.trim.TrimPolicy\") ke fungsi [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\").\n"

